# Vermilion Mesa: a figure-eight in red rock country (FORMAT.md).
#
# The first loop runs counter-clockwise round the mesa: out of the tunnel
# onto the floor of Vermilion Canyon, east along it on a broad flat arc,
# up the switchbacks in Aspen Draw on the mesa's east face, and west
# across the top through the pines. Over the tunnel the road leaves the
# mesa's west spur on a steep descent through fallen blocks, and the
# second loop runs clockwise round the arch valley north of the spur and
# back south into a long tunnel through the mesa's foot, under the road
# it has just driven.

track vermilion size 768 style redrock
title VERMILION MESA
blurb A figure-eight in red rock country: a broad sweep along a canyon floor, switchbacks up a ravine of aspens, a run through the pines on top of the mesa, a plunge through the boulders and a long tunnel through the mesa's foot.
race laps 3 rivals 3 vehicle kart
road 14.5
materials verge red_sand
land 30 1.5
hour 15.5

# The canyon floor and the arch valley: not quite level.
hill 470 560 90 -1         # a shallow dip in the canyon floor under the Vermilion Cliffs
hill 150 220 70 1.5       # a low rise in the middle of the arch valley
hill 110 470 80 2         # the floor rising toward the west end of the canyon

# The Rockfall: a broad fan of fallen caprock under the west end of the
# spur, 17 m over the floor, which the descent runs down.
plateau 47 45 226,300 228,392 186,402 150,372 120,330 100,290 94,252 112,236 150,250 192,268

# Vermilion Mesa, 32 m over the canyon floor, its cliffs falling over 5 m.
# The main body, a north-east arm that is the north wall of Aspen Draw, and
# the west spur the tunnel goes through, one outline. The draw (east of
# x 545 between z 280 and 440) and the slope west of the spur are left out:
# the road climbs onto the mesa there on ramps.
