# The climbs onto and off the mesa: the land is built up to the road, so
# neither climb is on a deck.
ramp 345 730 30
ramp 1070 1372 30

# The tunnel through the foot of the mesa, from the north face of the spur
# to its south face, lit and lined in the style's laid red stone, the road
# level at 31 all the way through. The mesa road crosses over its middle.
# The approach cuts eat about 20 m into each end, so the land covers
# about 150 m of it and the rest stands out as lined galleries.
tunnel 1642 1838 6

# Bends that bots took too fast and ran wide: the left turn off the
# canyon floor into the draw, the right-hand curve at the top of the
# descent, the left turn into the valley at its foot, the left turn
# onto the mesa at the top of the climb, and the curve out of the
# tunnel onto the canyon floor. Banked harder.
bank 270 380 2.2
bank 440 530 2.5         # hairpin A
bank 600 690 2.5         # hairpin B
bank 700 800 2
bank 1090 1230 2.2
bank 1330 1470 2.2
bank 1845 1935 2.2

# Two natural arches over the road: one spanning the canyon floor, one in
# the arch valley the second loop runs round.
arch 150 24 13 8 mat wingate_sandstone
arch 1500 26 15 9 mat navajo_sandstone

